\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 Wetlab Research\
Phase 1: $N = 1$ (You \'97 Hardware Dogfooding & Pipeline Engineering)
\f1\b0 \
  
\f0\b Goal:
\f1\b0  Build and stress-test the data pipeline on yourself until it is completely frictionless.\
\
   * 
\f0\b What You Build:
\f1\b0 \
       1. 
\f0\b The Ingestion Bridge:
\f1\b0  Write the Python script using brainflow or muse-lsl to stream raw EEG/fNIRS from the\
          Muse into a local SQLite/libSQL database on your laptop.\
       2. 
\f0\b The Apple Health Bridge:
\f1\b0  Export your Apple Health data (export.xml) and write a simple script to pull\
          continuous hourly HRV (RMSSD), resting heart rate, and sleep stages.\
       3. 
\f0\b The Financial Ledger:
\f1\b0  Tag your own bank/credit card due dates and paydays for the month.\
   * 
\f0\b What You Test on Yourself:
\f1\b0 \
       * 
\f2\i Signal Artifacts:
\f1\i0  Figure out how much forehead movement, swallowing, or blinking creates noise on channels AF7\
         and AF8.\
       * 
\f2\i Habit Friction:
\f1\i0  Determine the ideal 5-to-10 minute window (e.g., sitting quietly at your desk right after\
         paying a major bill vs. right after waking up).\
   * 
\f0\b Scientific Status ($N = 1$ Dense Time-Series):
\f1\b0 \
       * Even with $N = 1$, because you have 
\f0\b 30 days of continuous hourly Apple Watch data and daily EEG snapshots
\f1\b0 , you\
         can run 
\f0\b Granger Causality
\f1\b0  and 
\f0\b autocorrelation tests
\f1\b0 : 
\f2\i Does a bank account balance trough predict an HRV drop 12
\f1\i0 \
         
\f2\i hours later?
\f1\i0 \
\
  ---\
\
  
\f0\b Phase 2: $N = 10$ (The Pilot Cohort & Effect Size Calibration)
\f1\b0 \
  
\f0\b Goal:
\f1\b0  Prove the protocol works on other humans with different skull shapes, hair types, and financial stress levels.\
\
   * 
\f0\b Logistics:
\f1\b0 \
       * Recruit 10 friends, colleagues, or early supporters who already own an Apple Watch.\
       * Rotate your 
\f0\b 2 Muse headbands
\f1\b0  between them around their specific bill-due dates and post-paydays.\
   * 
\f0\b What You Accomplish:
\f1\b0 \
       1. 
\f0\b Estimate the True Effect Size:
\f1\b0  Calculate the empirical difference (Cohen\'92s d) in frontal theta/alpha and\
          overnight HRV between bill days and relief days.\
       2. 
\f0\b Run Non-Parametric Statistics:
\f1\b0  \
           * At $N = 10$, you do not rely on the Central Limit Theorem.\
           * Instead, you use the exact statistical methods already established in your research papers: 
\f0\b Wilcoxon
\f1\b0 \
             
\f0\b signed-rank tests
\f1\b0  and 
\f0\b 2,000-resample permutation tests
\f1\b0 .\
       3. 
\f0\b Run the First 5 Dyadic Pairs (Hyperscanning):
\f1\b0 \
           * Put two participants in the headbands simultaneously during a simulated negotiation or trust game to\
             record your first real 
\f0\b Inter-Brain Phase Locking (Kuramoto R)
\f1\b0  traces.\
\
  ---\
\
  
\f0\b Phase 3: $N = 30$ (The Confirmatory, Publishable Study)
\f1\b0 \
  
\f0\b Goal:
\f1\b0  Invoke the Central Limit Theorem, generate bell-curve projections, and publish/patent the findings.\
\
   * 
\f0\b The Milestones Unlocked at 30:
\f1\b0 \
       1. 
\f0\b Normality & Parametric Power:
\f1\b0 \
           * The Central Limit Theorem kicks in for your paired t-tests and Linear Mixed-Effects Models (LMM).\
           * Statistical power reaches 
\f0\b \uc0\u8805  85%
\f1\b0  for medium-to-large effect sizes (d \uc0\u8805  0.52).\
       2. 
\f0\b Academic Publication:
\f1\b0 \
           * $N = 30$ within-subject repeated measures gives you the statistical backing to publish an empirical\
             companion paper in top behavioral/neuroscience journals (
\f2\i Nature Human Behaviour
\f1\i0 , 
\f2\i NeuroImage
\f1\i0 , or\
             
\f2\i Psychophysiology
\f1\i0 ).\
           * It permanently eliminates the critique: 
\f2\i "The DOCAS framework is purely in-silico."
\f1\i0 \
       3. 
\f0\b The Commercial Moat for FreshCredit:
\f1\b0 \
           * You have 
\f0\b 900 subject-days of real human telemetry
\f1\b0  proving that financial stress creates measurable\
             executive depletion (C and D channel disruption), and that your on-device edge protocol successfully\
             protects user privacy while buffering vulnerability.\
\
  ---\
\
  
\f0\b Summary Checklist to Start Today
\f1\b0 \
\
   1. 
\f0\b Order 1 or 2 Muse S Athena headbands
\f1\b0  from choosemuse.com.\
   2. 
\f0\b Start Phase 1 immediately on yourself:
\f1\b0 \
       * Export your Apple Health data.\
       * Connect the Muse via Bluetooth to your Mac.\
       * Record a baseline 5-minute session today, and record another during your next big bill payment or major\
         financial transaction.\
   3. Once your Python scripts can ingest and merge your own Watch + Muse + Transaction dates automatically, you are\
      ready to hand headbands to your first 10 volunteers.\
